WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.067
Here we have a simple aggregate.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:09.847
The query groups survey responses by question and calculates the number of responses and the average score.

00:00:09.847 --> 00:00:13.077
Run it in the browser and check the grain.

00:00:13.077 --> 00:00:16.772
One output row represents one question.

00:00:16.772 --> 00:00:24.846
In Spark S Q L, the same grouping idea would apply, but the data could be distributed across many partitions.
